Everything under this directory comes from Movement Distribution, published
by AI for Good at Meta (formerly Data for Good at Meta) on the Humanitarian
Data Exchange:

  https://data.humdata.org/dataset/movement-distribution

HDX lists the dataset's licence as Creative Commons Attribution International
(CC BY, license_id cc-by); it is used here as CC BY 4.0.

Credit:

  Data for Good at Meta, Movement Distribution, Humanitarian Data Exchange
  (https://data.humdata.org/dataset/movement-distribution)

The files under movement-distribution/original/ are Meta's own, byte for
byte, including files HDX no longer lists; manifest.json records each one's
size, sha256 and dates.

The Parquet under movement-distribution/ was made from them:

  - the CSVs were combined into one table a year
  - rows that appear in two files (the same day, region and category, with the
    same values) were kept once, from the file HDX changed last
  - ds became a date, polygon_level an integer and
    distance_category_ping_fraction a double; the other columns are the text
    of the CSV
  - a source_file column was added, naming the original each row came from
  - rows were sorted by country, region, day and distance category
  - values were not changed

The code that fetches, checks and converts is MIT, in the repository this
dataset was built from (https://github.com/yuiseki/meta-move-dist), and does
not apply here.
